  "rationale": "The representative prefix ends in “with,” where the model overwhelmingly favors “a” because its existing determiner rule matches a final preposition. In the batch, the three “A day with …” prefixes are followed by different proper nouns, so add equal, context-specific mass for the available names rather than weakening the preposition-to-determiner rule globally; that rule remains useful for contexts such as “upon a.” This is a small output-only repair and avoids the complexity of the preceding rejected structural candidate. The unprompted short generation is diagnostic, not a label, and does not alone justify imposing story-framing constraints. A preposition “with” can also precede a non-person noun, and names beyond the declared vocabulary are not covered; the added evidence should therefore remain defeasible and be checked by replay.",
